RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
February 8, 2010
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS: Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne and Mr. Spiker.
Absent: Mr. Collins and Mr. Valdez.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City
Treasurer, and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Brown, and pursuant to support received by
Mr. Pierson and Ms. Broyles, agenda item #16(a) was removed from the Consent Agenda. Mr.
Brown moved to approve remaining Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Spiker. Motion
carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on January 25, 2010.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Vouchers Meeting of the Governing Body on February 1, 2010.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Spiker moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Ms. Broyles.
Upon inquiry, City Treasurer Barb Dorr reviewed information available for the following vouchers
payable to: Brown’s Shoe Company ($27.50), copying and administrative fees pursuant to Police
Dept. investigation records request; Reiman Corp. ($210,257.00), Carey/Pioneer rehab. construction
project; Top Shelf Enterprises LLC, ($2,800.00), removal and discarding of structural mold/moisture
damage; Lock Shop of Cheyenne Inc. ($510.00), after hours services for Police Dept.; W. G. Dale
Electric Co. ($140.00), telephone system changes (Transit office); Ellenbecker Oil Inc. ($24,311.61),
diesel fuel purchases (Fleet Maint., Street & Alley and Sanitation); VISA charge to Audubohn Intl.
($200.00), membership dues (Golf Director). Also providing additional information pursuant to
vouchers involved in discussion were: Doug Vetter, City Engineer; Captain Jeff Schulz, Interim
Police Chief; Jim Elias, Public Works Director, and Rick Parish, Parks and Recreation Director.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
“Ordinance amending Section 6.08.020 (B), Keeping or slaughtering of certain animals -
Restrictions within City, of Chapter 6.08, Animal care and control regulations generally, of Title 6,
Animals, and amending Section 6.20.010, Designation of Animal Shelter, of Chapter 6.20,
Impoundment, of Title 6, Animals, of the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming.”  Reporting for
Public Services Committee, Ms. Ash moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Dr.
Rinne. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present. (#3882)
```

