[CA]
Wyoming Children’s Trust Fund Grant Contract between the Wyoming Department of
Family Services, Protective Services Division, and City of Cheyenne, Special Friends - Youth
Alternatives, for the Special Friends Outreach Program -- referred to Finance Committee.
[CA]
Energy Performance Contract between the City of Cheyenne and Long Building
Technologies, Inc. to provide equipment and services designed to save energy at 52 City owned
facilities to include a  lighting retrofit, occupancy sensor installation, modular boiler in Fire Station
#1, an energy conservation education program and measurement and verification of energy savings
-- referred to Finance Committee.
 [CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and the Wyoming Department of State Parks &
Cultural Resources for a Land and Water Conservation Fund Grant for a basketball court in Martin
Luther King Park -- referred to Finance Committee.
Contract Modification No. 1 to Contract No. 5428 between the City of Cheyenne and Mill
Brothers Landscape and Nursery, Inc., Ft. Collins, CO, for additional irrigation and ground
preparation for Saddle Ridge Neighborhood Park (School Dist. Rec. Mill).  Reporting for Finance
Committee, Mr. Brown moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $9,825.88, seconded by Mr.
Spiker.  Mr Brown moved to amend by substitute, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Upon inquiry, Rick
Parish, Parks and Recreation Director, clarified an error in the wording contained in Section 1 of the
document was noticed following the Finance Committee meeting, and that the substitute corrects
the language.  He indicated completion of the project will include sodding and seeding of some
areas.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.  Main
motion as amended by substitute carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present.  (#5428)
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #M-11-10 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne and Reiman
Corp., for the East Cheyenne Greenway, Phase IIIb Project (1% Specific Purpose Sales & Use Tax).
Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried (amount not to exceed $358,328.55).  (#5513)
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-8-10 for the Surplus Sale of “Two 1993 Toro Greens Aerators”
from the City of Cheyenne Golf Department -- referred to Finance Committee.
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #M-13-10 for a Contract between S&S Builders, of Cheyenne, WY,
and the City of Cheyenne for the Randall Bridge Enhancements Project  (2007-2010 1% Sales Tax) -
referred to Finance Committee.
Appointment of Shane Moore, Gale Shenefelt, Charles Livermont, Daryl Hensel, Regina
Meena and Clayton Gray, to the Mayor’s Council for People with Disabilities. Ms. Broyles moved
to approve, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all members of the governing
body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote (Mayoral appointments).
Announcement was made of a Public Hearing to be held February 22, 2010 at 6:00 p.m. in
City Council Chambers for renewal of existing City Liquor Licenses (retail, restaurant, limited
